    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** as our premier option, boasting an elite 81.88 efficiency score. Despite facing a decent arm in Sandy Alcantara, **Gunnar Henderson** gains significant equity from a prime leadoff spot and a dynamic platoon advantage that pushes his ceiling well into the top tier. **Josh Lowe** (71.68) and **Heliot Ramos** (65.34) follow closely as high-upside plays; while both suffer from suboptimal batting order positions, their high sprint speeds and favorable matchups against pitchers with slow deliveries create massive stolen base potential\u2014a crucial factor given our league's scarcity-driven roster construction. **Miguel Vargas** also warrants attention, utilizing a significant SP skill edge against Aldegheri to reach a 66.77 score, bolstered further by wind-out conditions.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involved the exclusion of **Marcell Ozuna**, who sits on the bench with a 61.17 score. While **Marcell Ozuna** grades out as a strong start in most contexts, the sheer density of high-efficiency matchups for **Josh Jung** and our primary outfielders squeezed him out of the starting nine. We prioritized **Josh Jung** (64.67) due to his exceptional matchup against the 7.06 xERA of Eduardo Rodr\u00edguez, which provides more room for run production than the middle-of-the-order slotting assigned to **Marcell Ozuna**. Investors should monitor the status of **Drake Baldwin**, whose sub-50 efficiency against Kirby is dampened by a tough SP skill matchup; he remains in the lineup primarily for positional coverage, but he is at risk if his leadoff production stalls early. We are banking on the high-floor production of **Nolan Schanuel** and the speed-heavy profiles of our outfield to maintain our competitive edge in the 5x5 standings.",
